{"about":"9843f16c55a02ce422d04eb9057d52cb554dfe0052e19a3d19653ba96e18dc92","body":"The conjecture must not conflate 'rational decision' with 'probabilistic inference'; it is required to show exactly how acting on the best-tested theory is rational in Popper's specific sense (critical preference) without implicitly relying on the very inductive principle that past success predicts future reliability, which Popper explicitly rejected.","kind":"mini.commitment-proposal.v1","named":"The definition of rational action without induction"}